### 1. The Sustainability Datacenter Implementation

This class extends `PowerDatacenter` to act as the global facility manager. It tracks cumulative costs, applies escalating utility rates, and calculates carbon taxes.

```java
import org.cloudbus.cloudsim.power.PowerDatacenter;

public class SustainabilityDatacenter extends PowerDatacenter {
    // Methodology state based on your input-evaporative.txt
    private double cumulativeCarbonTax = 0.0;
    private double cumulativeWaterCost = 0.0;
    private double gridCarbonIntensity = 0.45; // kg CO2/kWh
    
    // Annual growth rates from your methodology
    private final double carbonTaxGrowth = 0.15; // 15% escalation
    private final double electricityInflation = 0.03; // 3% inflation

    @Override
    protected void updateCloudletProcessing() {
        super.updateCloudletProcessing();
        
        double currentTime = getSimulation().clock();
        double totalPowerKw = getPower() / 1000.0;
        int currentYear = (int)(currentTime / 8760); // 8760 hours in a year

        // 1. Dynamic Carbon Accounting (Scope 2)
        // Adjust grid intensity annually based on grid_decarbonization
        double currentIntensity = gridCarbonIntensity * Math.pow(0.95, currentYear);
        double hourlyEmissionsKg = totalPowerKw * currentIntensity;

        // 2. Carbon Tax Escalation ($50 -> $135/ton)
        double currentTaxRate = 50.0 * Math.pow(1.15, currentYear);
        this.cumulativeCarbonTax += (hourlyEmissionsKg / 1000.0) * currentTaxRate;

        // 3. Escalated Electricity Cost
        double escalatedRate = 0.12 * Math.pow(1.03, currentYear);
        double hourlyOpex = totalPowerKw * escalatedRate;
    }
}

```

